------------------------------ Nested routes and redirections ----------------------------------------


- A REAL APPLICATION OFTEN HAS NESTED ROUTES AND REDIRECTIONS.

- Instruction: Angular Prerequisite "Router" chapter (Advanced routing section)

- 🤩Currently, the races page only displays the pending races. We would like to show the finished
    races, too, in a separate tab.

1️⃣ Create two components pending-races and finished-races in the races directory:

        ng generate component races/pending-races --skip-selector
        ng generate component races/finished-races --skip-selector

    👉 The pending-races component should display what the races component currently shows.
    👉 The finished-races component should display all the finished races, the same way, but without
    the links to bet on the races.
    Both templates should also keep the same loading and error handling as the previous races
    list: display <div role="status">Loading.</div> while the resource is loading, and display
    <div class="alert alert-danger" role="alert">An error occurred while loading races.</div>
    if the loading fails.



2️⃣ To load the finished races, change the signature of the RaceService.list() method to
    RaceService.list(status: 'PENDING' | 'RUNNING' | 'FINISHED').
    race-service.ts:

        list(status: 'PENDING' | 'RUNNING' | 'FINISHED'): ResourceRef<Array<RaceModel> | undefined> {
            return httpResource<Array<RaceModel>>(() => ({
                url: `${environment.baseUrl}/api/races`,
                params: { status }
            }));
        }

    pending-races.ts and finished-races.ts:

        protected readonly races = inject(RaceService).list('PENDING');



2️⃣ The races component should display tabs (see the Bootstrap documentation to know how to
    generate tabs), and should use a nested router-outlet directive to display the active tab
    content.
    Regarding the routes:
    👉 /races should redirect to /races/pending;
    👉 /races/pending should show the pending races (and make the first tab, Pending races, active);
    👉 /races/finished should show the finished races (and make the second tab, Finished races,
        active).
    app.routes.ts:

        {
            path: 'races',
            canActivate: [loggedInGuard],
            children: [
            { path: '', component: Races,
                children: [
                { path: '', pathMatch: 'full', redirectTo: 'pending' },
                { path: 'pending', component: PendingRaces },
                { path: 'finished', component: FinishedRaces }
                ]
            },
            { path: ':raceId', component: Bet },
            { path: ':raceId/live', component: Live }
            ]
        }
    
    
    races.html:

        <h1>Races</h1>
        <ul class="nav nav-tabs mb-4">
            <li class="nav-item">
                <a class="nav-link" routerLinkActive="active" routerLink="pending">Pending</a>
            </li>
            <li class="nav-item">
                <a class="nav-link" routerLinkActive="active" routerLink="finished">Finished</a>
            </li>
        </ul>
        <router-outlet />
